notices and warning signs are relevant to the occupational area and associated equipment","parent":"102/1"},{"code":"102/1.7","kind":"criterion","title":"State why health, safety and welfare legislation, notices and warning signs are relevant to the occupational area","parent":"102/1"},{"code":"102/1.8","kind":"criterion","title":"State how to comply with control measures that have been identified by risk assessments and safe systems of work","parent":"102/1"},{"code":"102/2","kind":"outcome","title":"Recognise hazards associated with the workplace that have not been previously controlled and report them in accordance with organisational procedures","parent":"102"},{"code":"102/2.1","kind":"criterion","title":"Report any hazards created by changing circumstances within the workplace in accordance with organisational procedures","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/2.2","kind":"criterion","title":"List typical hazards associated with the work environment and occupational area in relation to: resources, substances, asbestos, equipment, obstructions, storage, services and work activities","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/2.3","kind":"criterion","title":"List the current health and safety executive top ten safety risks","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/2.4","kind":"criterion","title":"List the current health and safety executive top five health risks","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/2.5","kind":"criterion","title":"State how changing circumstances within the workplace could cause hazards","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/2.6","kind":"criterion","title":"State the methods used for reporting changed circumstances, hazards and incidents in the workplace","parent":"102/2"},{"code":"102/3","kind":"outcome","title":"Comply with organisational policies and procedures to contribute to health, safety and welfare","parent":"102"},{"code":"102/3.1","kind":"criterion","title":"Interpret and comply with given instructions to maintain safe systems of work and quality working practices","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.2","kind":"criterion","title":"Contribute to discussions by offering/providing feedback relating to health, safety and welfare","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.3","kind":"criterion","title":"Contribute to the maintenance of workplace welfare facilities in accordance with workplace welfare procedures","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.4","kind":"criterion","title":"Safely store health and safety control equipment in accordance with given instructions","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.5","kind":"criterion","title":"Dispose of waste and/or consumable items in accordance with legislation","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.6","kind":"criterion","title":"State the organisational policies and procedures for health, safety and welfare, in relation to:\n• Dealing with accidents and emergencies associated with the work and environment\n• Methods of receiving or sourcing information\n• Reporting\n• Stopping work\n• Evacuation\n• Fire risks and safe exit procedures\n• Consultation and feedback","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.7","kind":"criterion","title":"State the appropriate types of fire extinguishers relevant to the work","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/3.8","kind":"criterion","title":"State how and when the different types of fire extinguishers are used in accordance with legislation and official guidance","parent":"102/3"},{"code":"102/4","kind":"outcome","title":"Work responsibly to contribute to workplace health, safety and welfare whilst carrying out work in the relevant occupational area","parent":"102"},{"code":"102/4.1","kind":"criterion","title":"Demonstrate behaviour which shows personal responsibility for general workplace health, safety and welfare","parent":"102/4"},{"code":"102/4.2","kind":"criterion","title":"State how personal behaviour demonstrates responsibility for general workplace health, safety and welfare, in relation to:\n• Recognising when to stop work in the face of serious and imminent danger to self and/or others\n• Contributing to discussions and providing feedback\n• Reporting changed circumstances and incidents in the workplace\n• Complying with the environmental requirements of the workplace","parent":"102/4"},{"code":"102/4.3","kind":"criterion","title":"Give examples of how the behaviour and actions of individuals could affect others within the workplace","parent":"102/4"},{"code":"102/5","kind":"outcome","title":"Comply with and support all organisational security arrangements and approved procedures","parent":"102"},{"code":"102/5.1","kind":"criterion","title":"Provide appropriate support for security arrangements in accordance with approved procedures:\n• During the working day\n• On completion of the day's work\n• For unauthorised personnel (other operatives and the general public)\n• For theft","parent":"102/5"},{"code":"102/5.2","kind":"criterion","title":"State how security arrangements are implemented in relation to:\n• The workplace\n• The general public\n• Site personnel\n• Resources","parent":"102/5"},{"code":"234","kind":"unit","title":"Erecting masonry cladding in the workplace","optional":false,"level":2},{"code":"234/1","kind":"outcome","title":"Interpret the given information relating to the work and resources when erecting masonry cladding","parent":"234"},{"code":"234/1.1","kind":"criterion","title":"Interpret and extract relevant information from:\n• Drawings\n• Specifications\n• Schedules\n• Method statements\n• Risk assessments\n• Manufacturers' information","parent":"234/1"},{"code":"234/1.2","kind":"criterion","title":"Comply with information and/or instructions derived from risk assessments and method statements","parent":"234/1"},{"code":"234/1.3","kind":"criterion","title":"Describe the organisational procedures developed to report and rectify inappropriate information and unsuitable resources and how they are implemented","parent":"234/1"},{"code":"234/1.4","kind":"criterion","title":"Describe different types of information, their source and how they a